From 27d40ed2daac0ab97797eb633991518586027616 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mingmingzhichu <lihaoyu0717@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 16:36:59 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] usb: dwc3: keep Qualcomm glue DMA in the low 4 GiB

The controller advertises a 64-bit address width, so the driver normally
asks for a 64-bit mask.  On Qualcomm glue the interconnect only decodes
32-bit addresses: a 64-bit coherent allocation lets the ep0 TRB land
below the start of DRAM and the first controller DMA wedges the NoC.

Keep the original 64-bit mask everywhere else and restrict the low
4 GiB mask to the platforms whose glue node is compatible with
"qcom,dwc3".

Signed-off-by: mingmingzhichu <lihaoyu0717@outlook.com>
---
 drivers/usb/dwc3/core.c | 13 ++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc3/core.c b/drivers/usb/dwc3/core.c
index ee56148eb..5a5a1f6b5 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc3/core.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc3/core.c
@@ -2276,9 +2276,20 @@ int dwc3_core_probe(const struct dwc3_probe_data *data)
 	dev_set_drvdata(dev, dwc);
 	dwc3_cache_hwparams(dwc);
 
+	/*
+	 * The controller advertises a 64-bit address width, so the driver
+	 * normally asks for a 64-bit mask.  Qualcomm's glue only decodes
+	 * 32-bit addresses: a 64-bit coherent allocation lets the ep0 TRB
+	 * land below the start of DRAM and the first DMA wedges the NoC.
+	 */
 	if (!dev_is_pci(dwc->sysdev) &&
 	    DWC3_GHWPARAMS0_AWIDTH(dwc->hwparams.hwparams0) == 64) {
-		ret = dma_set_mask_and_coherent(dwc->sysdev, DMA_BIT_MASK(64));
+		if (of_device_is_compatible(dwc->sysdev->of_node, "qcom,dwc3"))
+			ret = dma_set_mask_and_coherent(dwc->sysdev,
+							DMA_BIT_MASK(32));
+		else
+			ret = dma_set_mask_and_coherent(dwc->sysdev,
+							DMA_BIT_MASK(64));
 		if (ret)
 			goto err_disable_clks;
 	}
